        1. Mandatory INPS Pension Contribution Rules for Freelancers (Gestione Separata)
      </h2>
      <p>
        The single most overlooked liability for remote workers relocating to Italy under the Digital Nomad Visa is <strong>INPS Gestione Separata</strong>. Unlike salaried employees whose employer pays the bulk of pension levies, independent contractors (liberi professionisti) bear the entire burden personally:
      </p>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
          <h4 class="text-white font-bold text-sm mb-2">Statutory Rate: 26.07%</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">
            Freelancers without a dedicated professional guild (ordine) must remit <strong>26.07%</strong> of their net taxable freelance earnings to the Italian National Social Security Institute (INPS).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
          <h4 class="text-white font-bold text-sm mb-2">Annual Massimale Cap (~€119,650)</h4>
